---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const updated = '2026-11-28';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What soloyolo collects (almost nothing), how cookies and advertising work, and the choices you control."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy policy' }]} />

    <article class="max-w-3xl pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.1rem,1.4rem+3.4vw,3.4rem)] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em]">
        Privacy policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
        Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time>
      </p>

      <div class="prose-ledger mt-10">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information soloyolo ("the site", "we") handles when you use the
          site, and the choices you have. The short version: the tools collect nothing on a server,
          the convenience data they keep stays in your browser, and you decide whether advertising
          cookies are used at all. soloyolo is operated by {SITE.operator}.
        </p>

        <h2>Information the tools collect</h2>
        <p>
          No server receives your numbers. Every calculator and document generator runs entirely in
          your browser. Income targets, expenses, hours, client names, addresses and invoice details
          are never uploaded, and there is no account.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some tools offer local convenience features, described under "Local storage" below. That
          data is written to this browser's storage on your device, is never sent anywhere, and
          disappears when you clear the site's storage.
        </p>

        <h2>Local storage</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses browser storage to remember choices and to make the toolkit feel like a
          desk. Nothing in this list is transmitted to us or to a third party.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent choice.</strong> <code>soloyolo-consent</code> records whether you chose
            <em>Accept all</em> or <em>Essential only</em>. It is a single technical value and holds
            no personal data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Theme choice.</strong> <code>soloyolo-theme</code> remembers Auto, Dark or
            Light.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Remembered tool inputs.</strong> The calculators keep the values and currency
            you last entered, and the payment reminder keeps its message fields, so a reload does
            not wipe your work. These are ordinary business figures, not client documents.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Business profile (opt-in).</strong> If you save a profile in a generator, your
            business name, address, registration number, payment details and optional logo are
            stored locally so the next document can reuse them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Desk data.</strong> The home desk can remember a print log (document type,
            number and total), recent tools, pinned tools, client names, weekly hours, a timer, a
            weekly goal and the market you selected. This is a local convenience record; there is no
            saved-document library and no cloud sync.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Session counters.</strong> <code>soloyolo-session</code> and
            <code>soloyolo-last-visit</code> hold a page count and a timestamp so the site can greet
            a returning visitor. They are local values only.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To remove all of it, clear site data for this domain in your browser settings. The tools
          keep working; they simply start from their defaults again.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics 4 to understand which tools and
          pages are useful. The Google tag is present on every page, but measurement storage is off
          by default: analytics and advertising storage are set to denied until you choose
          <em>Accept all</em> or tick <em>Anonymous measurement</em> in the cookie banner. With
          <em>Essential only</em>, no analytics or advertising cookies are set and no cookie-based
          measurement is used; Google may still receive a consent signal and a cookieless ping.
        </p>
        <p>
          When measurement is allowed, Google Analytics may collect the pages you view, the site you
          came from, your approximate location derived from your IP address, device and browser
          information, and interactions such as scrolling or outbound clicks. It does not receive
          the numbers you type into a calculator or the contents of a document. The data is used to
          improve the tools and the site, not to identify you.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can change your choice at any time by clearing this site's storage and choosing again,
          or by using the cookie banner on your next visit. Google also offers an opt-out browser
          add-on at
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout
          </a>
          .
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics and advertising cookies</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics cookies.</strong> Only if you choose <em>Accept all</em> or tick
            <em>Anonymous measurement</em>. Google Analytics may set cookies such as
            <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> to distinguish sessions and measure usage.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising cookies.</strong> Only if you choose <em>Accept all</em> in the
            cookie banner. When advertising is enabled, Google and its partners may set cookies to
            serve and measure ads, including personalised ads where allowed.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you choose <em>Essential only</em>, no analytics or advertising cookies are set and no
          advertising scripts load. The Google tag remains on the page in consent-denied mode, so no
          cookie-based measurement or personalised advertising is used.
        </p>

        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          The site displays ads served through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. When advertising is
          enabled:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior
            visits to this or other websites.
          </li>
          <li>
            Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on
            your visits to this and other sites.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can opt out of personalised advertising in
            <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Google Ads Settings
            </a>
            or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
            <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              aboutads.info
            </a>
            .
          </li>
          <li>
            Where local law requires consent, ads only load after you give consent, in line with
            Google's user consent policy.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Ads are clearly separated from content, are never disguised as tools or navigation, and do
          not influence which tools are built or how they calculate.
        </p>

        <h2>Server logs</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served statically through a hosting provider, whose infrastructure processes
          standard technical logs (for example IP addresses and request times) for security and
          abuse prevention. We do not use these logs to profile visitors. Analytics measurement is
          consent-gated as described above and does not receive the contents of your documents or
          calculator inputs.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal
          data, to object to processing, or to withdraw consent. Because the tools collect no
          personal data, most requests will simply concern your cookie choice: clear your browser
          storage for this site, or email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with "Privacy" in the
          subject line and we will help.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          The site is aimed at working professionals and is not directed at children under 13. We do
          not knowingly collect data from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If the tools, hosting or advertising set-up changes, this page will be updated and the
          "last updated" date above will change. Material changes to advertising or cookies will be
          reflected in the cookie banner as well.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
